        "title": "fix: guard setDeep against empty keys array in Chrome profile decoration",
        "body": "Related: #98465\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`setDeep()` with empty `keys` creates `obj[\"\"] = value` via `keys[-1] ?? \"\"`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd early `if (keys.length === 0) return;` guard.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change. Defensive guard.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Runtime terminal proof:**\n\n![screenshot](https://github.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/blob/proof-screenshots/pr-98138-proof.png?raw=true)\n\n- 36/36 tests passed (`profiles.test.ts`)",
